# keur quality control — a Python repo whose sonar-project.properties configures
# no coverage report path (Sonar then shows 0% coverage).
#
# Why this exists: for Python, Sonar reads coverage from a coverage.xml report
# via `sonar.python.coverage.reportPaths`. Miss it and coverage reads 0% and any
# coverage gate fails silently.
#
# HOW (requires + absence): `requires: lang: python` gates to repos containing
# Python (facts, ADR-009). The absence engine fires when the key appears
# NOWHERE. `content_contains: sonar.sources` skips files with no analysis.
#
# WARN, low confidence: coverage may be passed via CI or skipped on purpose.
# @see docs/rules-authoring.md
id: SONAR-007
ilities: [testability]
maturity: 3
title: Python repo — Sonar config has no coverage report path
category: quality
severity: warning
engine: absence
action: warn
confidence: 0.5
requires:
  lang: python
target:
  filenames: sonar-project.properties
  content_contains: sonar.sources
patterns:
  - regex: (?mi)^\s*sonar\.python\.coverage\.reportPaths\s*=\s*\S
    message: "Python repo: sonar-project.properties sets sonar.sources but no sonar.python.coverage.reportPaths — Sonar will show 0% coverage. Point it at your coverage.xml."
fix: "Add `sonar.python.coverage.reportPaths=coverage.xml`, and generate it with `coverage xml` (coverage.py) or `pytest --cov --cov-report=xml` before the scan."
